You are basically limited by your resources, the network stack can 
handle millions of connections.  The kernel memory required 
per-connection is below 2K (rough math here), so, how much memory do you 
have :)  That doesn't include any user processes and resources they 
require of course.

So if you have an ES47 with 4 cpus and 8GB of memory the sky is the 
limit; if you have a DS10L with 1 cpu and 512MB on the other hand...

-Brian


