I already have the answer.

The installation of Extended System V Functionality causes the
creation of the directory /usr/lib/nls/loc/iconvTable with some files
in it.

Worldwide Language Support, however, wants to create a symbolic link
to the directory /usr/i18n/lib/nls/loc/iconvTable in that place.

I had to deinstall Extended System V, remove the directory
/usr/lib/nls/loc/iconvTable and then install Worldwide Language
Support.

After that I could install Extended System V Functionality.

There is apparently an order in which you have to perform an
installation of the associated products. I wonder if any of this is
documented.

