TyBreaker wrote:

> I understand the gs80 is 8-CPU capable whereas the es47 is only 4-CPU
> capable so there are immediately questions of scalability if that interests
> you.

Take a look at http://www.kunhardt-computer.de/kunden/kch/achart.htm

Those guys are selling second hand Alphas and the chart is interesting. 
It appears that AS-4100 (ES-4x) family scales rather poorly with added 
CPUs - 4xCPU = from 3.17 to 2.77 effective CPUs. The lowest number is 
for the strongest CPUs, which might indicate that the main bus is a 
bottleneck. This might not be true of ES-47 machine, it is newer and so 
is the main board.

On the other hand, 8x00 family (GS-1xx) scales slightly better. If you 
need raw power in one place, go for GS. If it can be in two places, go 
for 2xES. If you need/like a cluster go for 2xES, plus cluster equipment 
(beware, it is costly and trivial to setup - the license alone is $40k).

Nix.


